{
  "_comment": "Curated map of normalized platform display names -> Twitch category names, for known mismatches (regional titles, 'GOTY Edition' naming, mod launchers) and for the creative/dev apps the install index surfaces. CategoryResolver tier 2 (DESIGN.md 1.5), loaded via CategoryResolver::loadAliasTable(), which normalizes both these keys and the game's own display name the same way (strip (tm)/(r)/(c), collapse whitespace, casefold) before comparing, so key casing here does not matter. TWO VALUE SHAPES. A plain string means 'switch to this category automatically', the same as it always did. An object with \"prompt\": true means OFFER it and never apply it on its own - the plugin raises the creative-app prompt instead (DetectionStateMachine PromptKind::CreativeApp). Every creative and dev app here is prompt-only on purpose: having Photoshop or VS Code open is not evidence that someone is streaming it, and is very often just a window left open from earlier. Auto-switching there would be the single most annoying thing this plugin could do, and it is also the case where asking costs nothing, because the app is not going anywhere. Real games that merely need renaming should use the plain string form. Community PRs against this file are the 'actually maintained' promise made concrete; see README.md and DESIGN.md Section 8.",
